<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RN's gradle plugin sets usesCleartextTraffic="false" in release builds
  (see AndroidManifest.xml's ${usesCleartextTraffic} placeholder), which by
  default blocks the "Sync from PC over wifi" feature in SettingsScreen --
  that flow talks to the analyzer's `serve` command over a plain http://
  URL on the user's LAN (see SettingsScreen.tsx: DEFAULT_SYNC_URL /
  onSyncFromWifi).

  A proper fix would scope cleartext to specific domains via
  <domain-config>, but the sync target is a LAN IP the user types in
  (e.g. http://192.168.x.x:8765/vibes.db) -- it varies per user/network and
  isn't a fixed hostname, so a domain allowlist isn't practical here.

  PRAGMATIC ALPHA CHOICE: allow cleartext traffic for all hosts. This app is
  sideload-only alpha, the only cleartext consumer is the opt-in LAN sync
  feature (nothing else in the app makes plaintext HTTP requests), and the
  traffic never leaves the local network in the intended use case.

  TODO: tighten this before any wider distribution -- either move wifi sync
  to https (self-signed cert pinning or a lightweight local CA step in the
  analyzer's `serve` command), or have the user paste just the LAN IP into a
  dedicated settings field and generate a <domain-config> entry for it at
  runtime/build time instead of allowing cleartext globally.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
